if Monocarp invites friends 4 and 6, they will eat all of the pizzas;

if Monocarp invites friends 5 and 6, they will quarrel because of the 3-rd pizza.

In the first test case, there is only one permutation with length n=1 that is p=[1], which is not perfect:

p1=1=x2 for x=1.

In the second test case, one possible perfect permutation with length n=4 is p=[2,4,1,3]:

p1=2≠x2;

p1+p2=2+4=6≠x2;

p1+p2+p3=2+4+1=7≠x2;

p1+p2+p3+p4=2+4+1+3=10≠x2.

In the third test case, one possible perfect permutation with length n=5 is p=[5,1,4,3,2]:

p1=5≠x2;

p1+p2=5+1=6≠x2;

p1+p2+p3=5+1+4=10≠x2;

p1+p2+p3+p4=5+1+4+3=13≠x2;

p1+p2+p3+p4+p5=5+1+4+3+2=15≠x2.

In the first test case, you cannot delete any element. The array remains [2,1,4,5,2] and is p-towering for p=3 by picking i=4:

a1=2≥p−|i−1|=3−|4−1|=0;

a2=1≥p−|i−2|=3−|4−2|=1;

a3=4≥p−|i−3|=3−|4−3|=2;

a4=5≥p−|i−4|=3−|4−4|=3;

a5=2≥p−|i−5|=3−|4−5|=2.

In the second test case, you can remove the first, second, and fifth elements to obtain the array [4,5]. Clearly, the obtained array is p-towering for p=5 by picking i=2.

On the first test case, the given region is [0,1]×[1,2]. There is one node accounting for [0,1]×[1,2]. Choosing this node, the answer is 1.

On the second test case, the given region is [0,2]×[0,2]. There is one node accounting for [0,2]×[0,2]. Choosing this node, the answer is 1.

On the third test case, the given region is [1,3]×[1,3]. There is no node that accounts for [1,3]×[1,3]. Instead, you can make the union of regions exactly the same as [1,3]×[1,3] by choosing the following 4 nodes:

A leaf node accounting for [1,2]×[1,2];

A leaf node accounting for [1,2]×[2,3];

A leaf node accounting for [2,3]×[1,2];

A leaf node accounting for [2,3]×[2,3].

It can be shown that it is impossible to make the union of regions exactly the same as [1,3]×[1,3] with less than 4 nodes. Therefore, the answer is 4.

On the fourth test case, the given region is [0,2]×[1,5]. You can make the union of regions exactly the same as [0,2]×[1,5] by choosing the following 5 nodes:

A leaf node accounting for [0,1]×[1,2];

A leaf node accounting for [1,2]×[1,2];

A non-leaf node accounting for [0,2]×[2,4];

A leaf node accounting for [0,1]×[4,5];

A leaf node accounting for [1,2]×[4,5].

It can be shown that it is impossible to make the union of regions exactly the same as [0,2]×[1,5] with less than 5 nodes. Therefore, the answer is 5.

